The presence of this file indicated that the gravity constant of Hillsboro will be used when determining the calibration of the load cells
containing the Accelerometer. The difference of the gravity constant between Hillsboro, OH and Troy, OH is partly determined by the elevation of
each location above sea level.  The difference of elevation, in addition to latitude, longitude is enough to make the gravity constant 
different between the two places.

Troy Gravity Constant      = 980104
Hillsboro Gravity Constant = 980023

To use the Hillsboro, OH, gravity constant, the default, rename this file as 'gravity_hillsboro.dat' and reboot.
To use the Troy, OH gravity constant, rename this file as 'gravity_troy.dat' and reboot.

The existence of this file alone indicates the gravity constant to be used while calibrating the accelerometers, not any text contained within it.